CTOX repository notice

This repository contains first-party CTOX code plus integrated hard forks
and integrated per-model inference trees.

Primary integrated source trees:

- src/core/transfers/aria2-rust
  Unchanged tracked-source snapshot of https://github.com/mkh-welsch/aria2-rust at
  8364bcd7902dbd853a0f746c3dc937bbaadec561 (based on 7bfacc2cf27e55d4755b06623c1b997880d0c697).
  License: GPL-2.0-or-later, per its retained original LICENSE and Cargo.toml.
  Original copyright notices and tests are retained. The owner authorized this
  in-tree redistribution; builds do not require private upstream Git access.
  PROVENANCE.json records the source tree and SHA-256 of each imported file.

- src/harness
  Derived from https://github.com/openai/codex
  Upstream license: Apache-2.0
  Integrated into CTOX as a source-owned hard fork and driven in-process
  by CTOX's agent turn loop. Previously lived at src/inference/.

- src/inference/models/<model>/
  Per-model self-contained inference crates. Each crate carries its own
  Rust inference code plus its own vendored kernel source (CUDA/Metal)
  in-tree. Upstream vendored kernel provenance is pinned per crate in
  `vendor/*.version` files. No code is shared across model crates.

The previously-carried Candle-based `tools/model-runtime/` subtree has
been retired.

- tools/web-stack/assets/humanlike.mjs
  Behavioral primitives (mouse Bezier curves, typing latency model with
  nearby-key mistypes, three-phase burst-wheel scrolling, actionability
  gating) are reimplemented in JavaScript from the open-source Python
  wrapper of https://github.com/CloakHQ/CloakBrowser (MIT, Copyright
  CloakHQ). Only the wrapper algorithms are ported; the patched-Chromium
  binary is not used and not redistributed.

- tools/web-stack/assets/stealth_init.js
  JS-property evasions (navigator.webdriver proxy, realistic plugins/
  mimeTypes shaped like real Chrome 2024+, window.chrome runtime/csi/
  loadTimes, permissions.query notification consistency, WebGL
  UNMASKED_VENDOR/RENDERER platform mapping, iframe.contentWindow
  propagation, hardware concurrency, languages, outer dimensions, plus
  Function.prototype.toString patching) are ported from the open-source
  evasions in
  https://github.com/berstend/puppeteer-extra/tree/master/packages/puppeteer-extra-plugin-stealth
  (MIT, Copyright berstend and contributors).

- runtime/browser/interactive-reference/ (operator workspace)
  CTOX drives Chromium through Patchright
  (https://github.com/Kaliiiiiiiiii-Vinyzu/patchright-nodejs, Apache 2.0),
  a drop-in Playwright fork that patches Runtime.enable, Console.enable,
  and source-URL CDP leaks. The package is installed at runtime into the
  operator workspace via `npx patchright install chromium` and not
  bundled into the CTOX distribution.

- src/apps/business-os/modules/desktop/ and src/apps/business-os/shared/
  Portions of these directories derive from OSKO
  (https://github.com/cmdkolab/osko, MIT) at commit
  475cddd5539d8eeb6ec1b86dbe1e57db8d1c03b7. The OSKO-derived code has been
  refactored into its CTOX-native form and is owned and maintained by CTOX.

- src/apps/business-os/office-engine/
  Contains the CTOX-native browser port boundary for selected Euro-Office
  document and spreadsheet editor sources. Euro-Office is an AGPL-3.0 fork of
  ONLYOFFICE. The exact release, submodule revisions, image digest, excluded
  product surfaces, and update policy are pinned in
  `office-engine/upstream/euro-office-v9.3.1.json`. The pinned DocumentServer
  image is a development oracle only and is not part of the CTOX runtime.

- src/apps/business-os/assets/provider-logos/
  Provider artwork copied from the local Workjet project
  (https://github.com/metric-space-ai/claude-workjet), whose source code and
  artwork are distributed under the MIT license, Copyright (c) 2026 metric
